  "id": "observational-learning",
  "term": "observational learning",
  "definition": "Observational learning is learning to reproduce an action by watching another person perform it. In this source, it is described as a largely strategic process in which the observer uses visible cues and known task constraints to infer how the movement should be coordinated, even when only limited motion information is available.",
